Clinical Interventions: Prescribed immediate strong oral opioid analgesia (e.g., oxycodone 5mg every 4-6 hours as needed) to control the severe bony pain. Provided a marked, urgent referral for comprehensive blood tests in the morning (including PSA, CMP, FBC) and an urgent referral to a Urologist and Medical Oncologist.
Positive Behavioral Change: (Not applicable in an acute, likely terminal/oncological diagnostic crisis requiring urgent specialist intervention; focus is on immediate pain control and system navigation).
Home-Based Services (Optional): None.
DME/Safety (Optional): Urgently advised strict rest to prevent pathological fractures of the spine or pelvis.
Follow-up: Mandatory GP review within 24-48 hours to execute the urgent referrals and review the PSA and imaging results.

